("v25", "key", "prompt")
("v26", "type", "String")
("v26", "scalar", "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: a panoramic three-panel comic illustration for a literary personal website essay, titled Power Must Serve Life, with a handwritten correction to AI. Create one coherent triptych with exactly THREE equally sized narrative panels side by side, separated by narrow irregular ink rules, filling a very wide landscape composition. Mixed graphite, ink, wax crayon and watercolor on luminous warm parchment. Rich emerald and teal, vivid terracotta, ochre gold, cream paper; crisp expressive linework, visible crayon grain, sophisticated editorial graphic-novel style. Repeat the same ordinary adult protagonist with short dark hair and a terracotta jacket across all panels. PANEL ONE on left: the person sits at a wooden table with sketches, notebooks and a small unlabelled computing device, authoring a purposeful idea; a window shows an enclosed dark geometric tower beyond. PANEL TWO centre: the person and a collaborator examine and revise a physical map-like composition of translucent geometric shapes and paths on the table; the protagonist points to an alternative and moves a piece, expressing real choice and correction. Represent machine assistance through quiet luminous geometry, never a humanoid robot. PANEL THREE on right: the person carries an open portfolio into a bright garden workshop, sharing their creation with a small group of people who are making their own things, with room and independent activity around them. The arc is from purpose through accountable assistance into retained capability and shared life. Treat this as an imagined scene, not an advertisement or proof of a technology. Warm, lively, human, specific, with storytelling gestures and beautiful settings. No text, no lettering, no captions, no speech balloons, no logos, no watermarks. Keep all key characters and actions inside their own panels. No dramatic saviour figure, no worship of a machine. Full illustration, not a website screenshot.")
("v25", "value", "v26")
("rel.document", "root", "v0")
